# Changelog (monthly batching)

When editing [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md):

## `[Unreleased]`

- **Only** the experimental new-games bullet (and nothing else long-term).
- Do **not** park shipped QoL, fixes, or production-visible work under `[Unreleased]`.

## Dated `[1.0.0-ci]` sections

- **One section per calendar month** (e.g. all October 2026 work under a single `## [1.0.0-ci] - YYYY-MM-DD`).
- **Never** add a second dated header in the same month for routine commits (no `2026-10-04`, `2026-10-17`, `2026-10-19`, … alongside each other).
- When adding a bullet this month:
  1. Find the existing section whose date is in the **same calendar month and year** as today.
  2. If found: append under the correct `### Added` / `### Changed` / `### Fixed` / `### Removed` heading and **update only that section’s date** to today (`YYYY-MM-DD`).
  3. If none exists: create **one** new section below `[Unreleased]` with today’s date.
- Merge bullets from duplicate same-month sections if you find them; delete the extra headers.

## Do not

- Copy the entire changelog from another branch commit without applying monthly consolidation.
- Put production-shipped items only under `[Unreleased]` when `main` already carries them.

See also [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) (Changelog) and the intro paragraph at the top of `CHANGELOG.md`.
